{"uid":"a060185ecd964f56","name":"test_an_unsettled_message_is_withheld_until_a_non_steer_iteration_completes","fullName":"tests.test_steer#test_an_unsettled_message_is_withheld_until_a_non_steer_iteration_completes","historyId":"2a0f32e54e8827f7f35d535b822378c1","time":{"start":1791919247442,"stop":1791919247614,"duration":172},"description":"Task 014 (PRD requirement D.4, #184): the defect this task fixes,\n    demonstrated end to end. Before this task, `_handle_unsettled_steering`\n    unconsumed the message on the spot, so `worker`'s absolute-top-priority\n    guard (`if self.run.pending_steering(): -> steer`, task 012) forced the\n    very next pass straight back into `steer` -- turning one operator\n    message no hat can settle into `1 + steer_redelivery_max` consecutive\n    `steer` iterations with nothing else ever running in between. This test\n    drives the real drain path (`_run_iteration_once`'s own tail, exercised\n    here via `run_iteration(\"worker\", ...)` directly, exactly the way\n    other modules already call `run_iteration` without going through\n    `_step_worker`'s own scheduling) and shows the message stays withheld\n    across as many CONSECUTIVE steer passes as are attempted -- well past\n    the declared cap -- and is handed back out only once a genuine\n    non-steer iteration has run to completion.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014 (PRD requirement D.4, #184): the defect this task fixes,<br />\ndemonstrated end to end. Before this task, <code>_handle_unsettled_steering</code><br />\nunconsumed the message on the spot, so <code>worker</code>'s absolute-top-priority<br />\nguard (<code>if self.run.pending_steering(): -&gt; steer</code>, task 012) forced the<br />\nvery next pass straight back into <code>steer</code> -- turning one operator<br />\nmessage no hat can settle into <code>1 + steer_redelivery_max</code> consecutive<br />\n<code>steer</code> iterations with nothing else ever running in between. This test<br />\ndrives the real drain path (<code>_run_iteration_once</code>'s own tail, exercised<br />\nhere via <code>run_iteration(&quot;worker&quot;, ...)</code> directly, exactly the way<br />\nother modules already call <code>run_iteration</code> without going through<br />\n<code>_step_worker</code>'s own scheduling) and shows the message stays withheld<br />\nacross as many CONSECUTIVE steer passes as are attempted -- well past<br />\nthe declared cap -- and is handed back out only once a genuine<br />\nnon-steer iteration has run to completion.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791919247429,"stop":1791919247429,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791919247429,"stop":1791919247434,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791919247434,"stop":1791919247434,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791919247435,"stop":1791919247438,"duration":3},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_wait_out_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791919247438,"stop":1791919247438,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"att